OBJECTIVE:

Clean up the local Git repository and push pending changes
back to the remote Git repository.
1. CHECK MASTER STATUS
git checkout master
git status
Make sure the master branch is in a clean state.
2. LIST ALL BRANCHES
git branch -a
3. PULL REMOTE REPOSITORY
git pull origin master
This gets the latest changes from the remote repository
into the local master branch.
4. PUSH PENDING CHANGES
git push origin master
This pushes the pending local changes to the remote
Git repository.
5. VERIFY REMOTE REPOSITORY
Open the GitLab repository in the browser.
Check whether the latest changes are visible in the
remote repository.
COMPLETE FLOW
Check master status
       ↓
git status
       ↓
List branches
       ↓
git branch -a
       ↓
Pull remote changes
       ↓
git pull origin master
       ↓
Push pending changes
       ↓
git push origin master
       ↓
Check GitLab
       ↓
Verify changes are reflected
git status
    → Check repository status
git branch -a
    → List local and remote branches
git pull origin master
    → Get latest changes from remote

git push origin master
    → Upload local changes to remote
KEY POINT:
PULL  = Remote → Local
PUSH  = Local → Remote
